            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "LGTM. I will +1 after the conflict is resolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuDevice.cpp",
                    "line": 50,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: Could we add a quick comment on where 30s comes from? NSM spec doesn't\ndefine polling rate, so a brief budget note would help future maintainers:\n\n  // 30s long-running poll interval. Per-device SerialQueue serializes all\n  // long-running cmds; each holds the slot for up to 2s (TTIMEOUT_LONG\n  // worst case). Worst-case capacity ~ 30s/2s = 15 cmds per device.\n\nNo strong opinion if you'd prefer a different framing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuDevice.cpp",
                    "line": 50,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaLongRunningHandler.hpp",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: Could we add a quick comment on the 2s value? NSM Base Spec v1.2.0\nspecifies TTIMEOUT_LONG = 1s for long-running event delivery, so something\nlike the following would help future maintainers understand the choice:\n\n  // Per NSM Base Spec v1.2.0 (TTIMEOUT_LONG = 1s), long-running events\n  // arrive within 1 second of cc=ACCEPTED. This timer uses 2s as a 2x\n  // defensive margin against transport/firmware jitter.\n\nSame note in the commit message would also be nice. No strong opinion if\nyou'd prefer to keep it as-is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaLongRunningHandler.hpp",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
